> A gastric bypass changes gut hormones involved in hunger, fullness and blood sugar control. Some patients may see blood-sugar changes early after surgery, but the extent, timing and duration of any improvement vary between individuals; your treating doctors will explain what to expect.

Source: extracted draft L175-L185 and L191-L193.

