docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:191:> Expected weight loss: 70-80% of excess weight, clinical average; results vary. Time in surgery: about 120 minutes under general anaesthetic using a keyhole technique. Hospital stay: usually 2-3 nights. Return to most activity: about 3-4 weeks, with light duties often sooner and heavy lifting later.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:305:> At OSWA, gastric bypass patients are assessed by bariatric surgeons including Dr Harsha Chandraratna (MBBS, FRACS) and Dr Stephen Watson (MBBS, FRACS), who perform keyhole bariatric procedures and guide patients through suitability, risks, preparation and follow-up.
