docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:383:> Compared with open surgery, keyhole surgery may reduce wound size and support recovery for suitable patients, but pain, scarring and recovery time vary and complications can still occur. Your surgeon will confirm whether a keyhole approach is appropriate for you.
